<h2 id="doors" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">4. What each door failure means</h2>

<table>
<thead>
<tr style="background:#1565c0;color:white"><th>Door</th><th>Question (freshman)</th><th>Fail label</th><th>Which paragraph(s) to autopsy</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td style="background:#e3f2fd">A</td><td style="background:#fff3e0">Can we generate the first 5 pool units twice?</td><td style="background:#ffebee"><code>failed_first5</code></td><td style="background:#e8f5e9">Every <code>AGENT_JUDGE tier=over_budget</code> (or hard FAIL) row in the Door A / first-5 sections that prevented the door from passing. Prefer the <b>last</b> failing <code>id</code> per attempt wave if many; if several distinct units exhausted budget, autopsy <b>each</b>.</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#e3f2fd">B</td><td style="background:#fff3e0">Can we generate the whole pool once?</td><td style="background:#ffebee"><code>failed_all</code></td><td style="background:#e8f5e9">Every <code>over_budget</code> / FAIL row in the ALL-WORDS section that blocked shipping. Autopsy <b>each</b> distinct <code>id</code> that exhausted attempts (not only the first).</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#e3f2fd">C</td><td style="background:#e8f5e9">After A+B shipped, did <b>both</b> quality judges mark every paragraph <code>OK</code>?</td><td style="background:#fff3e0"><code>quality_failed</code></td><td style="background:#e8f5e9">Every <code>result.failed_ids</code> entry (<code>scope#pN</code>). Any single-judge <code>ISSUE</code> fails the paragraph. Use <code>warnings</code> / <code>split_verdict</code> when judges disagree.</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

**Ids:**

- Door A/B harness: `scope` + row `id=` (DB / pool row id in `[pglpl-live] AGENT_JUDGE … id=N`).
- Door C: `scope#pN` = **Nth Door B snapshot paragraph** (1-based), not necessarily DB `row_id`. Match snapshot `text` / `row_id` back into the ALL-WORDS log.

**If zero fails** in the request: say so in the header and stop (no empty play-by-play inventing).

