<h2 id="shape" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">7. Response shape (mandatory)</h2>

Write for a **college freshman**.

### 7.1 Run header

| Field | Value |
|-------|--------|
| Run | `§6.xx` |
| Log / Door C JSON | paths |
| Wall | seconds if known |
| Requested scopes | list or “all failing” |
| Failures in request | Door A: …; Door B: …; Door C: … **or** none |

### 7.2 Index (≥2 targets)

| Door | Scope | Unit (`id` / `#p`) | One-line cause |

### 7.3 One section per failing paragraph

Heading: **`[Door X] scope id=N` — one-line cause** (or `scope#pN` for Door C).

**Header strip (2–4 lines, before the attempt table):**

| Field | Value |
|-------|--------|
| Required blanks | listed surfaces / hosts |
| Standing produce cue | smallest prompt line that shaped the contract (optional if irrelevant) |
| Final outcome | `over_budget` / `template_fallback` / Door C `both_issue` / … |

**Attempt matrix (mandatory for multi-attempt Door A/B fails):** one HTML table (`mrkd` colors). **Rows = attempts** (`r1`…`rN`, chronological). Columns stay short but must surface the **problematic** bit:

<table>
<thead>
<tr style="background:#1565c0;color:white"><th>Attempt</th><th>Produced (clip to clash)</th><th>Verify</th><th>Injection Gate</th><th>Other (LWM / punch / local rewrite)</th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td style="background:#e3f2fd">r1</td><td style="background:#e8f5e9">… <code>o amapaense</code> …</td><td style="background:#fff3e0"><code>ok:false</code> — invented tilde / spelling fight</td><td style="background:#ede7f6">n/a or Keep/missing/wrong_gender one-liner</td><td style="background:#fff8e1">—</td></tr>
<tr><td style="background:#e3f2fd">r5</td><td style="background:#ffebee">… <code>acraense</code> …</td><td style="background:#fff3e0"><code>ok:false</code> — wants <code>acreano</code></td><td style="background:#ede7f6">—</td><td style="background:#fff8e1">budget exhausted</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>

**Column rules:**

- **Produced** — quote only the span that matters (wrong spelling, bad stack, gender clash); full paragraph only if short.
- **Verify** — `ok:true/false` + one-line reason (truncate mid-essay reasons).
- **Injection Gate** — Keep / Still missing / Wrong gender one-liner, or `n/a` when that scope/phase did not run.
- **Other** — local gate rewrite (`uma artista`→`o artista`), punch miss, sense-anchor, etc.; use `—` when idle.
- Drop a column only if **every** attempt has nothing for it; never drop Attempt / Produced / Verify for A/B loops.

**Door C** (single shipped snapshot): one row is enough — Produced = snapshot `text` clip; Verify columns can hold Pair A / Pair B ISSUE lines instead of in-loop verify; Injection Gate usually `n/a`.

**Cause row / footer:** after the attempt matrix, 1–3 sentences: why this door failed (freshman-plain). Optionally one **pgjudge**-style flake vs real line inside Cause.

**Ineffective:** a Step/What/Evidence table that collapses five retries into one “Produce / Verify” row and hides how the draft got worse.

### 7.4 Optional wrap-up (multi-para)

Same root cause vs different roots — 2–4 sentences. No patch unless asked.

