<h2 id="related" style="color:#1565c0;font-size:1.22em;font-weight:650;border-left:4px solid #42a5f5;padding-left:10px;margin-top:1.1em">9. Related rules</h2>

| Rule | Owns |
|------|------|
| **`pgbattest`** | Run Door A/B/C campaigns |
| **`pgjudge`** | Short live A/B flake-vs-fix after `AGENT_JUDGE` (pgpbp may reuse its judgment **inside** the table) |
| **`pgtestcom`** | Run `pgbattest` + write scoreboard tip + compare vs prior `§6.xx` (`pgtestcom-pgbattest-compare-and-scoreboard.mdc`) — use when you need a **new** run, not autopsy of an old one |
| **`serlog`** | Read gitignored `logs/` / `llm_traffic` |
| **`evalay`** | Opinion-only gloss |
| **`traunit` / `trabat`** | Conj PLGW — different pipeline |

**Ineffective (avoid):**

- Stopping at “no Door C fails” when Door A/B failed (unless `doors:C` only).
- Replacing the play-by-play table with a bare `pgjudge` 1–2–3.
- Dumping full prompts or guessing text without log / snapshot evidence.
- Starting a new `pgbattest` from `pgpbp` alone.
